error[E0790]: `echo` cannot print a `secret` value
  --> 07-a-secret-in-the-output.nvs:7:6
  |
7 | echo "Bearer {******}\n";
  |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this value is `secret`
  = help: Output is read by people and saved in logs. To print the value anyway, call `Core\Secret::reveal($value, "reason")` first. Joining it into a longer string does not help. The result is `secret` too.

error[E0724]: a `secret`-qualified value cannot be passed to `Core\Debug::dump`; a dump is written to be read by a person, so the value would be disclosed rather than used
  --> 07-a-secret-in-the-output.nvs:8:18
  |
8 | Core\Debug::dump($token);
  |                  ^^^^^^ secret value dumped here
  = help: reveal it explicitly first with `Core\Secret::reveal(..., "reason")`; a `secret`-typed *property* of a dumped object needs nothing — the record redacts it

error[E0791]: a `secret`-qualified value cannot be passed to `Core\Json::encode`; an encoded document is on its way to a response, a log or a queue, and none of those is the credential being used
  --> 07-a-secret-in-the-output.nvs:9:24
  |
9 | echo Core\Json::encode($token), "\n";
  |                        ^^^^^^ secret value encoded here
  = help: reveal the one field that must travel with `Core\Secret::reveal(..., "reason")`, written at that field rather than at the call, so the rest of the value stays covered

